                "senderName": "NWS Wichita KS",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 13 at 2:15AM CDT until October 14 at 10:00AM CDT by NWS Wichita KS",
                "description": "* WHAT...Localized flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central, east central, south central, and\nsoutheast Kansas, including the following counties, in central\nKansas, Marion and McPherson. In east central Kansas, Chase. In\nsouth central Kansas, Butler, Harvey, Kingman, Reno and Sedgwick.\nIn southeast Kansas, Allen, Greenwood and Woodson.\n\n* WHEN...From late this afternoon through mid-morning Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in localized flooding of\nrivers, creeks, streams, city streets, underpasses, and other\nlow-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Scattered to numerous thunderstorms with high rainfall rates are\nexpected to move east to northeast across the same areas late\nthis afternoon through tonight. Areas of heavy rainfall are\nexpected, which could lead to localized flooding concerns.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
